EXAMPLE_ONLY_NOT_A_REAL_KEY_replace_with_INDEXNOW_KEY_env_value

# IndexNow key file format (example — NOT a real key, safe to commit)
#
# IndexNow lets a site notify Bing and Yandex that specific URLs changed.
# It is NOT a Google indexing mechanism — Google does not support IndexNow.
#
# The real key file must:
#   - be named exactly "<key>.txt" (e.g. a3f1c9...txt)
#   - live at the site root so it is publicly fetchable at https://<host>/<key>.txt
#   - contain ONLY the key string itself (no comments, no whitespace)
#
# How the real key is provisioned (no secret in git):
#   1. Generate a key (32+ hex chars), e.g. `openssl rand -hex 16`.
#   2. Set it as the Vercel env var INDEXNOW_KEY (Production).
#   3. At build/deploy time, scripts/ping-indexnow.mjs writes public/<INDEXNOW_KEY>.txt
#      dynamically from that env var. The real key file is never committed.
#
# This .example file documents the format only and contains no real secret.
